    "Burn-down list for scripts/ci/feedback-rules/secdef-function-grants.ts.",
    "Each entry is a public SECURITY DEFINER function whose defining migration does NOT",
    "explicitly REVOKE EXECUTE from anon and authenticated. On Supabase, ALTER DEFAULT",
    "PRIVILEGES grants those roles EXECUTE directly at CREATE time and REVOKE ... FROM",
    "PUBLIC does not remove a direct role grant, so each of these is potentially an",
    "anon-reachable RLS-bypassing RPC until verified against the live ACL.",
    "",
    "THIS LIST MAY ONLY SHRINK. Adding an entry means shipping a new instance of a class",
    "that has already caused five incidents (0364, 0377, 0378, 0388, 0406) - do not add,",
    "fix the migration. A stale entry (one that no longer violates) fails the test, so the",
    "list cannot silently re-authorise a regression.",
    "",
    "Grandfathered != safe. These are UNREVIEWED. Burning one down means checking the live",
    "prod ACL with has_function_privilege(anon, fn, EXECUTE) and either adding the REVOKE",
    "or moving the function to DELIBERATELY_PUBLIC in the rule with a reason.",
    "",
    "BURNED DOWN VIA REPLAY PARITY (0418). Four entries left this list without their",
